      "id": "PAS-01",
      "anchor": "normalization-period-ascent",
      "title": "The identity contribution in the initial separating period",
      "statement": "For ε and CF≥6510, beyond a common scale threshold and with the grid hypotheses, every nonzero row t has a cusp form y in the core at stage zero whose bottom period is nonzero on suitable vectors. Its Poincaré series has identity contribution cφ(x), with |φ(x)|>b/2 and c≠0, while all other cosets together have absolute contribution at most b|c|/2.",
