      "correspondence": "The source chooses the real test packet before t, then a height point x and a bound b for the evaluation of that row. Q is the packet loss, f counts the real places of the totally real field, and R uses the absolute norm of the congruence ideal. Long is an inequality on the product of norms for each nonzero ideal multiple.",
