      "title": "A prescribed smooth input and alternating nonzero periods",
      "statement": "Given a nonzero row t and prescribed nonzero smooth w, one can use a compact-finite core vector for the initial period and choose a reachable column chain. For even m≥2, nonvanishing propagates through Fourier–Jacobi periods at indices 2k+1 and Bessel periods at 2k+2. At each step the new datum is compatible with the earlier partial row lift.",
