    {
      "id": "PAS-03",
      "anchor": "normalization-period-ascent-factor",
      "title": "One archimedean factor from separately proportional Bessel tests",
      "statement": "Under the threshold, signature and weight-gap hypotheses at the last vertex, for a fixed smooth input w the tested period has the form A_w(ρ,ξ)l(t,c,Φ). A local rank bound of one, a product identity on pure tensors and spanning of both coefficient spaces give the factorization. Row-wise nonvanishing then makes one real pair work across the nonzero rows.",
